        "id": "synth_step_1",
        "type": "synthesis",
        "name": "Interphase Stabilization",
        "procedure": "Hou et al. applied this concept to anion-exchange membrane electrolyzers. The authors used metal-alkoxide (zirconium propoxide) additives that covalently bonded to the ionomer through polymerization. This created a layer of organic-inorganic interphase (zirconium oxo and hydroxo oligomer) between the ionomer and the anode catalysts. The interphase exhibited structural motifs that protected the ionomers from electrochemical degradation.",
